.TH WERKMEISTER-WORKFLOW-EXPORT 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-workflow\-export \- Write an ICM workspace's stages as a workflow folder (workflow.yaml + stages/)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister workflow export\fR <workspace>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-to <dir>\fR
A missing or empty folder to write the workflow into
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Writes an ICM workspace's stages as a workflow folder: \fBworkflow.yaml\fR and one \fBstages/<name>.md\fR per stage, read from the workspace's \fBstages/NN_<name>/CONTEXT.md\fR, the root \fBCONTEXT.md\fR and \fBCLAUDE.md\fR. It drops what werkmeister adds to each contract (the \fB## Pre\-approved\fR section, step \fB0.\fR, the ask\-tool line and the standards line) and turns this workspace's stage paths, worktrees and reload line back into the workflow variables \fBat:<stage>\fR, \fBrepos\fR and \fBrestart\fR (each written in double braces). Hand edits to the contracts are kept.
.PP
\fB<workspace>\fR is a workspace name, as \fBwerkmeister workspace list\fR prints it, or a path (\fB.\fR or anything with a \fB/\fR). It refuses a workspace that isn't icm, or a \fB\-\-to\fR folder that exists and isn't empty. Before it finishes, it loads the folder as \fBworkspace init\fR would, and removes what it wrote if that fails.
.PP
An autonomous workspace never rendered its human checks, so each exported stage uses its self\-check as the human check, and the command warns.
.PP
Put the folder at \fB~/.werkmeister/workflows/<type>/\fR or \fB<repo>/.werkmeister/workflows/<type>/\fR to use it: see "Adding your own workflow" in \fBdocs/icm\-workflows.md\fR. A repo's workflow may not grant \fBworkspace serve:*\fR or \fBpr autosquash:*\fR; the command warns when the export carries them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister workflow export sw\-1079\-workflow\-export \-\-to ~/.werkmeister/workflows/review
werkmeister workflow export . \-\-to ../review\-workflow
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
